=== X. 17 CFR 240.15c1-7: Discretionary accounts ===
official caption typography is Discretionary accounts.
15c1-7(a): The term manipulative, deceptive, or other fraudulent device or
  contrivance, as used in section 15(c) of the Act, is hereby defined to include
  any act of any broker, dealer or municipal securities dealer designed to effect
  with or for any customer's account in respect to which such broker, dealer or
  municipal securities dealer or his agent or employee is vested with any
  discretionary power any transactions or purchase or sale which are excessive in
  size or frequency in view of the financial resources and character of such
  account.
15c1-7(b): The term manipulative, deceptive, or other fraudulent device or
  contrivance, as used in section 15(c)(1) of the Act, is hereby defined to
  include any act of any broker, dealer or municipal securities dealer designed
  to effect with or for any customer's account in respect to which such broker,
  dealer or municipal securities dealer or his agent or employee is vested with
  any discretionary power any transaction of purchase or sale unless immediately
  after effecting such transaction such broker, dealer or municipal securities
  dealer makes a record of such transaction which record includes the name of
  such customer, the name, amount and price of the security, and the date and
  time when such transaction took place.
official typography italicizes the defined term, including the trailing comma,
  and does not put quotation marks around it: The term <I>manipulative,
  deceptive, or other fraudulent device or contrivance,</I> as used in official
  (a) and official (b); this toy does not invent quotes, and does not copy
  packed 15c2-4 typographic quotes
  onto this rule
official (a) cites "section 15(c) of the Act" without "(1)", while official (b)
  cites "section 15(c)(1) of the Act"; this toy does not tidy official (a) by
  inserting "(1)"
official (a) typography is "any transactions or purchase or sale which are
  excessive" (official grammar; this toy does not tidy it) and "or his agent or
  employee"
official (b) typography is "the name, amount and price of the security" (no
  Oxford comma) and "immediately after effecting such transaction" (no numeric
  clock); a straight apostrophe in "customer's account."
